            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "This dataset contains the do files for replicating the analyses in “Peers’ race in adolescence and voting behavior”.\n\nThe paper uses data from the National Longitudinal Study of Adolescent to Adult Health (Add Health), a program project directed by Kathleen Mullan Harris and designed by J. Richard Udry, Peter S. Bearman, and Kathleen Mullan Harris at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, and funded by grant P01-HD31921 from the Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human development, with cooperative funding from 23 other federal agencies and foundations. Special acknowledgment is due Ronald R. Rindfuss and Barbara Entwisle for assistance in the original design. Information on how to obtain the Add Health data files is available from the Add Health website (http://www.cpc.unc.edu/addhealth). No direct support was received from grant P01-HD31921 for this analysis. \nIn order to (purchase the access to) the data, you need to contact the Carolina Population Center: http://www.cpc.unc.edu/projects/addhealth. While part of the data is accessible for free, in the paper we make use of restricted access data.\nWe use the In-Home and In-School surveys for Wave 1 and the surveys in Waves III and IV. We also use the following additional data: from Wave I - School Network, Friend Files, School Distance Measures, and School Administrator Questionnaire; from Waves I and III - Contextual Files, Political Files; from Waves I, III and IV: Weight Files."
                }
              }
            ]
